Ladybird seeds a new profile’s languages from the platform’s
preferred-languages list, keeping the first entry and its language
subtag. Chrome’s default for its intl.accept_languages pref is the
localized IDS_ACCEPT_LANGUAGES string, "en-US,en" for an English UI
(components/language/core/browser/language_prefs.cc). Firefox sets
intl.accept_languages to "und" in all.js and replaces it with the
locale’s intl.properties value, "en-US, en" for en-US. WebKit’s
NavigatorBase::languages() returns WTF’s userPreferredLanguages(),
the system’s own list.
